# Outreach AI Cortex — Project Rules

## Stack
- Python 3.12, FastAPI, SQLAlchemy 2.0 (async), PostgreSQL 16, ChromaDB
- Dependency management: Poetry (pyproject.toml)
- Containerization: Docker Compose ONLY (no Kubernetes/k3s/Minikube)
- LLM calls: cloud APIs only (OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, OpenRouter)

## Hardware Constraints (CRITICAL)
- Target machine: 8 GB RAM, Intel Iris Xe (128 MB VRAM)
- NEVER suggest local AI models (Ollama, transformers, PyTorch, TensorFlow)
- Docker images: slim/alpine only; total container RAM ≤ 4 GB
- ChromaDB: minimal persistence, no heavy indexing on dev

## Project Structure
```
backend/app/
├── api/routers/     # HTTP endpoints (thin layer, no business logic)
├── core/            # config, database, security, dependencies
├── models/          # SQLAlchemy ORM models
├── schemas/         # Pydantic request/response schemas
├── services/        # Business logic (called by routers)
└── main.py          # FastAPI app factory, lifespan, router registration
```

## Naming Conventions
- Files: snake_case (`health.py`, `user_service.py`)
- Classes: PascalCase (`UserService`, `HealthResponse`)
- Functions/variables: snake_case
- Constants: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE
- API routes: kebab-case URLs (`/api/v1/health`, `/api/v1/outreach-campaigns`)
- Router prefixes: `/api/v1`

## Code Standards
- Type hints on ALL function signatures (Python 3.12 syntax)
- Docstrings: Google style for public functions/classes
- Async everywhere: async def routes, AsyncSession for DB, httpx for HTTP
- No business logic in routers — delegate to services/
- Pydantic v2 for schemas, pydantic-settings for config
- SQLAlchemy 2.0 style: select(), no legacy Query API

## Docker Rules
- Base image: python:3.12-slim (NOT alpine for Python — musl breaks asyncpg wheels)
- Always use depends_on with condition: service_healthy
- Always define healthcheck for every service
- Set mem_limit on each container

## Forbidden
- Local LLM inference
- Sync SQLAlchemy in new code
- Hardcoded secrets (use .env + pydantic-settings)
- Committing .env file
- kubernetes/helm/minikube mentions
